title The loop restarts on the lift work, steered by the card rather than by the recipe
prompt restart the loop on the caravan lift work
think Read the launcher before reaching for it. tools/launch-claude-season.rish PRINTS the recipe and does not launch -- its own words: the jail launch belongs in your outer terminal. So restarting the loop is two halves, and only one of them is mine. Mine is making the tree say the right thing; Keaton's hand runs the command.
think The recipe's prompt is one long baked line that names no specific door. It does name crux/REMEMBER.md as the first thing read after the voice files. That is the steering wheel, and it is the half I can turn -- so the way to point the loop at the lift work is to name the door in the card, not to retype the recipe.
think Declined to edit the recipe's prompt line, because the tree already ruled on that: to evolve the loop, fill a fresh version rather than editing these lines from memory. Filled recursion-prompts/versions/20260821-204005_autonomous-loop-caravan-lift.md instead, which is the sanctioned shape and leaves the elder line intact.
think Checked the route docs the recipe names by path before handing it over, since a loop that begins by failing to read its own route is worse than one that begins idle. All three resolve under active-designing/date/ -- the repointer reached the launcher's own prompt line during the fold, which is exactly what it was built to do and is pleasant to see proven from the far end.
think Wrote the prohibitions into the filled prompt as plainly as the invitations. No ascending mark, since fold AJ is the single most likely thing an unattended lap would type; do not repoint dated testimony, which is the resolver's whole distinction; do not raise a ceiling to make a meter green, which is the one way today's census could be quietly undone.
obs The prompt carries the three arc teachings rather than the three arc summaries -- read the harness before the meter, a visibility split is sometimes meaning, a cohort is measured at the head of the lap (REDS %111). A teaching survives into work a summary does not.
obs Named the carry meter's two numbers, because the loop will meet a meter that now reads carry and CARRY_DELEGATES=2365 and a reader who expects one number will think it broke.
obs Kept the GATES-ONLY clause exactly as it stands. The custody gates are the reason unattended running is safe at all, and this round had no business softening them.
loom route_docs=3 resolved=3 launcher_prompt_repointed=yes jq=present
loom guards_checked=3 recursion_prompts_census=green living_card_ascii=green e123_living_pin=green
file recursion-prompts/versions/20260821-204005_autonomous-loop-caravan-lift.md the filled prompt naming the lift as the first door, with the teachings and the prohibitions
file crux/REMEMBER.md THE FIRST DOOR row, so the card the loop reads first names the lift work chosen rather than a door left open
recommend check-in (Keaton) the tree is pointed and the recipe is printed, and the last step is a hand in the outer terminal on purpose. Worth watching one lap before letting it run to the deadline -- the card, the filled prompt, and the mark law all landed today, and one observed lap is the cheapest proof they read the way they were written.
